# GridGuard AI - Project Architecture & Coding Standards

## 1. Executive Stack Summary
- **Edge Device Simulator:** C++ (GCC/Clang, modern C++ standard) using JSON & MQTT (Eclipse Paho) libraries.
- **Backend API & AI Engine:** Python 3 (FastAPI/Flask) running natively on Linux.
- **Database:** SQLite for metrics, anomaly flags, and intrusion logs.
- **Frontend Dashboard:** HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, and Chart.js for real-time visualization.
- **Infrastructure & Virtualization:** Docker containerized MQTT Broker (Eclipse Mosquitto with TLS & JWT authentication).

---

## 2. Codebase Directory Structure
Ensure all generated code follows this exact project layout:
```text
gridguard-ai/
├── edge_simulator/      # C++ Edge Device Simulation
│   ├── src/             # Core C++ source files
│   └── include/         # Header files & config
├── backend/             # Python API Backend & AI Logic
│   ├── app/             # FastAPI/Flask application
│   └── database/        # SQLite schema & DB initialization
├── dashboard/           # Frontend Web Interface
│   ├── css/
│   ├── js/              # Chart.js & dynamic DOM updates
│   └── index.html
├── docker/              # Infrastructure Containerization
│   └── mosquitto/       # MQTT Broker TLS/JWT config
└── docs/                # Project documentation & APIs